==English==

===Etymology===
Medieval English vernacular form of [[Lucia]], name of a Sicilian martyr, from the {{etyl|la}} feminine form of the Roman [[praenomen]] [[Lucius]], from {{term|lux|lang=la}} "light".

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-Lucy.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|uːsi}}

===Proper noun===
{{wikipedia}}
